# .xal/strip-terms — terms that belong to the product this factory was extracted from, and
# must never ship in it. Read by gate 8 in scripts/check.sh as one ERE per line, matched
# case-insensitively as whole words across every tracked file.
#
# WHY: everything here is lifted by hand from a private estate (docs/lift-ledger.md). The
# failure this gate exists for is quiet: a unit name, a person or a private credential name
# left in a lifted script reads fine to its author, because it is true at home, and ships to
# every adopter. "Xal" itself is the brand and is allowed.
#
# Closed list. Add a line when a term leaks or plausibly would, never remove one without a
# lift-ledger note saying why it is now safe.

# the product's units (repositories)
xal-(auth|org|invoicing|notify|app|company|platform|site|onboarding|contacts|workspace)
# the operating layer and its plugin
xcos(-core)?
# the person at the gates; adopters name their own with factory.escalation_label
sodiq
needs-sodiq
# private credential names (adopters get FACTORY_* names)
XAL_(READ|PROJECT)_TOKEN
# product requirement and decision ids
ORG-FR-?[0-9]*
# personal locale
lagos
